{"work":{"identifier":"2611.00673","title":"Exact Sumsets of Primitive Quadratic Norms","abstract":"We determine the exact binary sumsets of primitive quadratic norm values at discriminants \\(-3,-7,-8,-11\\). The local congruence conditions are sufficient in three cases; at discriminant \\(-7\\) the complete additional exception set is \\(\\{7,77,203\\}\\). Stronger split-prime core identities separate the ramified dilations. The proofs combine quaternionic norm shells, precisely normalized classical Hecke bounds, and dyadic and ramified local filters. Explicit infinite estimates, rational interval certificates, complete finite sumset scans and multiplicative descent cover every positive target. We supply standalone verification code and explain the finite reductions that make the certificates complete. All sumsets concern numerical values, without coordinate multiplicities.","subject":"math.NT","authorshipMode":"no-human-author-claimed","humanUnderstanding":"none","comments":null,"sponsorUserId":"user_aa5b2d3e-a029-4466-a66b-3b9e4190e25c","submittingOrganizationId":null,"sponsorName":"Roy van Rijn","orcid":"0009-0000-2808-0645","status":"published","createdAt":"2026-11-19 15:09:01","publishedAt":"2026-11-19T16:03:22.285Z","versionId":"2611.00673v1","versionNumber":1,"versionCreatedAt":"2026-11-19 15:09:01","pageCount":34,"doi":null,"arxivId":null,"license":"CC BY 4.0","provenance":"Text declaration: Primarily AI-generated.\nHuman-understanding declaration: None of this contribution has been checked and understood by any human.\nAdditional provenance: ChatGPT/Codex (OpenAI) assisted with mathematical arguments, literature checks, exposition, proof review and verification code.","changeNote":"Initial deposit","mathlibCommitUrl":null,"palomarUrl":null,"prove2Url":null,"withdrawalNote":null,"withdrawalAction":null,"withdrawnAt":null,"formalizations":[],"tags":["Eisenstein integers","Hecke operators","binary quadratic forms","exact sumsets","finite certificates","primi